{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>מְצַחֵק אֵת רִבְקָה.</b> Meaning: an act of affection performed between a man and his wife. And according to the one who says (Genesis Rabbah 64:5) ״מְצַחֵק״ means he was preparing his bed — perhaps it was by one of the methods that is permitted even during the day, as for a medical purpose, as the Rambam wrote (Hilkhot De'ot, chapter 4), or like the incident recounted in the Talmud (Ketubot 65a) of the wife of Abaye who uncovered herself, etc., and Rava went, etc. — for the righteous are scrupulous even about something that merely resembles improper behavior, so as not to stumble in it."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:43:30.431390460Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}